.th NROFF I 1976
.sh NAME
nroff  \*-  format text
.sh SYNOPSIS
.bd nroff
[ options ] [ files ]
.sh DESCRIPTION
.it Nroff
formats text according to control lines embedded
in the text files.
.it Nroff
reads the standard input if
no file
arguments are given.
An argument of just ``\-'' refers to the standard input.
.s3
The options, which may appear in any order so long as they
appear before the files, are:
.s3
.ft I
.lp +9 8
option	meaning
.ft R
.s3
.lp +9 8
\fB-o\fIlist\fR	Print only pages whose page numbers appear
in \fIlist,\fR which consists of comma-separated numbers and number ranges.
A number range has the form \fIN-M\fR and means pages \fIN\fR through \fIM\fR;
a initial \fI-N\fR means from the beginning to page \fIN\fR;
and a final \fIN-\fR means from \fIN\fR to the end.
.s3
.lp +9 8
\fB-n\fIN-\fR	Number first generated page \fIN\fR.
.s3
.lp +9 8
\fB-s\fIN\fR	Stop every \fIN\fR pages.
\fINroff\fR will halt prior to every \fIN\fR pages
(default \fIN\fR=1)
to allow paper loading or changing, and will resume upon receipt of a newline.
.s3
.lp +9 8
\fB-m\fIname\fR	Prepends the macro file \fB/usr/lib/tmac.\fIname\fR to
the input \fIfiles\fR.
.s3
.lp +9 8
\fB-r\fIaN\fR	Register \fIa\fR (one character) is set to \fIN\fR.
.s3
.lp +9 8
\fB-i\fR	Read standard input after the input files are exhausted.
.s3
.lp +9 8
\fB-q\fR	Invoke the simultaneous
input-output mode of the \fBrd\fR request.
.s3
.lp +9 8
\fB-T\fIname\fR	Specifies the name of the output terminal
type.
Currently defined names are \fB37\fR
for the (default) Model 37 teletype, \fBtn300\fR for the
GE TermiNet 300 (or any terminal without half-line capabilities),
\fB300S\fR for the DASI-300S, \fB300\fR for the DASI-300, and
\fB450\fR for the DASI-450 (Diablo Hyterm).
.s3
.lp +9 8
\fB-e\fR	Produce equally-spaced words in adjusted lines,
using full terminal resolution.
.i0
.dt
.s3
Each option is invoked as a separate argument; for example,
.s3
	\fBnroff -o\fI4,8-10 \fB-T\fI300S \fB-m\fIabc file1 file2\fR
.s3
requests formatting of pages 4,8,9 and 10 of a document contained in files
named \fIfile1\fR and \fIfile2\fR, specifies the output terminal as a
DASI-300S, and invokes the macro package \fIabc\fR.
.s3
.it Nroff
may be used as a filter.
.sh FILES
.dt
/usr/lib/suftab	suffix hyphenation tables
.br
/tmp/ta#	temporary
.br
/usr/lib/tmac.*	standard macro files
.br
